+/* Hades: Dolby Vision Low-Latency ("player-led"), for a display that takes Dolby Vision only so
+ * (DVBRIDGE_DV_LOW_LATENCY_LAB, NV_HDMI_DV_LOW_LATENCY). The player maps the picture to the display:
+ * dvbridge_render_rgb() draws it mapped as dvbridge_render_hdr10() draws it with the same mapping (the
+ * curve guided by each scene's level 1 metadata, the perceptual gamut mapping, the black of the source
+ * kept, nothing above the display's peak), to the target that mapping gives: the peak and the gamut
+ * of the display's Dolby VSVDB (DVBRIDGE_HDR10_GAMUT_CUSTOM). dvbridge_render_pack() packs it as
+ * YCbCr 4:2:2 at 12 bits in the converted transport's layout, with no metadata in the chroma LSBs
+ * (the display management is done). Only the composed way: dvbridge_render_packed() refuses, and
+ * dvbridge_render_direct_fits() says no. Not the source transport: the picture is the mapped one, in
+ * BT.2020. Nothing else of a render changes (the step-down levels, the composer, the bars written
+ * first). NULL turns it off, the default; a mapping that is not valid, off or not to HDR10 is not
+ * taken: it turns it off, and the call returns false. The renderer keeps it through resets. */
+#define DVBRIDGE_RENDER_LOW_LATENCY 1
+bool dvbridge_render_set_low_latency(struct dvbridge_renderer *renderer,
+                                     const struct dvbridge_hdr10_mapping *mapping);
+bool dvbridge_render_low_latency(const struct dvbridge_renderer *renderer);
+/* Hades: with Low-Latency on, a test pattern instead of the picture, for the first look at a display
+ * (the tunnel's layout as the display reads its Low-Latency input): from the top, in quarters of the
+ * raster, eight BT.709 bars at 100 cd/m2 (white, yellow, cyan, green, magenta, red, blue, black) in
+ * BT.2020; a grey ramp from black to the display's peak; a staircase of luma codes 1024 to 1279, one
+ * code every 15 pixels, grey; and staircases of chroma codes, Cr 1920 to 2047 on the left and Cb 2048
+ * to 2175 on the right, at luma code 1536. The GUI is drawn over it as over a picture. */
+void dvbridge_render_set_ll_pattern(struct dvbridge_renderer *renderer, bool pattern);
